# Autonomous 3D Reference & Topology Researcher (`autonomous-3d-reference-researcher`)

## When to Use
- Before or during any 3D modeling task (characters, animals/creatures, firearms, vehicles, foliage, architecture) where guessing proportions from memory risks producing an inaccurate or "cartoony" model.
- When encountering a complex surface material (e.g., feline tapetum lucidum eye refraction, anisotropic fur velvet, parkerized steel gunmetal, subsurface skin scattering) that benefits from verified real-world physical constants.

---

## 1. Closed-Loop Online Research -> 3D Sculpt -> Self-Evolve Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["3D Modeling Task Started"] --> B["Web Search: Real-World Anatomy / Blueprints / bpy Recipes"]
    B --> C["Extract Concrete Ratios & Physical Constants (IOR, Angles, Dimensions)"]
    C --> D["Apply to Headless Blender 5.2 Script + Render 2x2 Contact Sheet"]
    D --> E["Verify Silhouette IoU & Visual Realism"]
    E --> F["Persist New Ratios/Recipes into Skill via skill-evolve"]
```

---

## 2. Mandatory Pre-Sculpt Web Research Protocol
Never guess anatomical or mechanical dimensions from memory. Before authoring vertex coordinates:
1. **Query Real-World Proportions (`search_web` / `read_url_content`):**
   - *For Animals/Creatures:* Search osteology/veterinary proportions (e.g., `"domestic cat skeletal proportions skull length to body length ratio scapula stifle hock angles"`).
   - *For Weapons/Vehicles:* Search exact technical specifications (e.g., `"AK-74M receiver length barrel length handguard dimensions mm"`).
   - *For Foliage/Trees:* Search botanical leaf arrangement (phyllotaxis), trunk taper ratios, and bark furrow patterns.
2. **Query SOTA Blender 5.x `bpy` Procedural Recipes:**
   - If a procedural part (e.g., cat ear concha helix, fur card normal transfer, procedural iris shader) needs higher realism, search for modern Blender `bpy` / Geometry Nodes / Shader Node techniques.

---

## 3. Verified Physical & Anatomical Reference Baseline (Built-In)

| Subject / Material | Verified Real-World Proportions & Shader Constants |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Domestic Cat (`Felis catus`)** | Shoulder height `~24 cm`, body length (chest to ischium) `~46 cm`, skull length `~9.0 cm` (`1:5` skull-to-body), cranial width `~6.8 cm`, muzzle length `32%` of skull, hock (calcaneus) height `35%` of hind leg height, inter-ocular distance `~38%` of head width. |
| **Cornea & Eye Optics** | Cornea `IOR = 1.376`, Roughness `= 0.01`, Clearcoat `= 1.0`, inner iris concave depth `= 1.5 mm` behind cornea dome (creates realistic parallax gaze). |
| **Mammalian Skin / Nose / Ear Pinna** | Subsurface Weight `= 0.35`, Subsurface Radius `= (1.0, 0.35, 0.2)`, Roughness `= 0.32` (rhinarium wet nose tip `= 0.12`). |
| **Pelted Fur (Anisotropic Rim)** | Base Roughness `= 0.55`, Sheen Weight `= 0.85`, Sheen Roughness `= 0.30` (simulates microscopic hair cuticle forward/backward grazing scatter). |

---

## 4. Automatic Crystallization Rule (`skill-evolve`)
Whenever online research yields a verified proportion table or `bpy` technique that visibly improves the 3D model, **immediately persist it** before finishing the turn:
```bash
skill-evolve --append-rule <target-3d-skill> "<Subject> Verified Proportions" "<compact table or bpy snippet>"
```

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform Blender 5.2+ Parity (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- **Executable Discovery:** Resolve Blender via `shutil.which("blender")` or fallback on Windows to `C:\Program Files\Blender Foundation\Blender 5.2\blender.exe -b --factory-startup`.
- **Cross-OS Scratch & OptiX Baking:** Stage intermediate `.blend`, `.png`, and `.ogf`/`.glb` exports in `Path(tempfile.gettempdir())` (`%TEMP%` on Windows, `/dev/shm` on Linux) and enable `compute_device_type = "OPTIX"` on both Windows WDDM 3.2 and Linux NVIDIA drivers.
